# Releases

Human versioning policy: [DEVELOPER.md](../../DEVELOPER.md) § Releases.

**Coordinated release rounds** are the [`release-round` skill](../skills/release-round/SKILL.md). This rule is the seatbelt when editing CHANGELOGs, `package.json`, or release scripts. CLI flags and auth live in the script headers; CHANGELOG craft in [changelog.md](../skills/release-round/changelog.md).

Major (breaking) rounds and nightlies need a dedicated procedure. Fork `--scope` publishes (not this skill): see the `release-npm.ts` header.

## Do not

- Publish to npm unless the human explicitly asked in this session.
- Run `npm publish` outside `scripts/release-npm.ts` unless the human directs otherwise.
- Skip hooks (`--no-verify`) or weaken `prepublishOnly`.
- Invent the active package list from README — use `ACTIVE_PACKAGES` in `scripts/release-npm.ts`.
- Commit tokens or `_authToken` entries.

## Active vs deps-only

**Active** (`ACTIVE_PACKAGES`): version bump + publish in `PUBLISH_ORDER`. **Deps-only** (`client`, `devp2p`, `ethash`, `wallet`, `testdata`): update `@ethereumjs/*` refs only; own version unchanged; not published.

All active packages share the **same new version number** on each round.

## CHANGELOG include / omit

Update **every** active package `CHANGELOG.md`, even with no user-facing changes.

**Include:** user-facing behavior, API, or defaults; Node/TS support; external (non-monorepo) dependency bumps.

**Omit entirely:** docs-only; `examples/`-only; tests-only; lint, spellcheck, CI, or other tooling-only PRs.

**No included PRs:** still add a version section with `Maintenance release, no active changes`.
